  DeepSwap's on-chain program (programs/deep-amm in the DEEP repository) is a fork of that code;
  programs/deep-amm/NOTICE there lists its modifications.

Ported here (re-implemented in TypeScript; no upstream file is copied verbatim):
  src/raydium-cpmm.ts     <- states/pool.rs, states/config.rs (PoolState / AmmConfig layouts),
                             PDA seeds, curve/{calculator,constant_product,fees}.rs
                             (swap_base_input quote), instructions/swap_base_input.rs (accounts)
  src/cpmm-liquidity.ts   <- curve/constant_product.rs lp_tokens_to_trading_tokens,
                             instructions/{deposit,withdraw}.rs (accounts and rounding)
  src/cpmm-initialize.ts  <- instructions/initialize.rs (accounts, initial LP, lock amount)
  src/cpmm-token2022.ts   <- utils/token.rs (supported mint extensions, transfer fee helpers),
                             instructions/swap_base_input.rs (transfer-fee order of operations)
  src/deep-amm.ts         <- instructions/admin/*.rs (accounts and args), states/
                             creator_fee_share.rs, curve/fees.rs (creator fee split)
  src/amm-events.ts       <- states/events.rs (SwapEvent layout)
  src/pairs.ts            <- SwapEvent interpretation (amounts, fees, reserves after a swap)

Changes: written from scratch in TypeScript with BigInt integer math; where upstream panics or
unwraps, these functions throw. The Squads v4 decoders (src/squads.ts) are re-derived from the
public account layouts, contain no Squads code and are MIT.
